WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.115
Let's make Make a little snowman.

2
00:00:02.495 --> 00:00:07.146
Pack three small snowballs, stack them low and add a pressed face with removable

3
00:00:07.146 --> 00:00:07.810
twig arms.

4
00:00:08.190 --> 00:00:10.270
Make this project with a grown-up.

5
00:00:10.650 --> 00:00:13.380
Gather the supplies listed below the video.

6
00:00:13.760 --> 00:00:16.005
Pause whenever you need more time.

7
00:00:16.385 --> 00:00:21.662
An adult checks the weather, clothing and safe location away from roads, water, roof

8
00:00:21.662 --> 00:00:23.170
edges and falling ice.

9
00:00:23.550 --> 00:00:27.520
Keep the snowman about 30 centimetres tall and stop for warm-up breaks.

10
00:00:29.000 --> 00:00:30.190
Step 1.

11
00:00:30.570 --> 00:00:32.590
Test a handful of snow.

12
00:00:32.970 --> 00:00:35.760
With mittens on, squeeze a small handful.

13
00:00:36.140 --> 00:00:39.065
If it holds together, use that snow.

14
00:00:39.445 --> 00:00:43.600
If it remains powdery, switch to a flat snow picture rather than adding hot

15
00:00:43.600 --> 00:00:44.490
water or salt.

16
00:00:44.870 --> 00:00:46.250
Grown-up help.

17
00:00:46.630 --> 00:00:49.090
Choose a safe area and check conditions.

18
00:00:50.500 --> 00:00:51.680
Step 2.

19
00:00:52.060 --> 00:00:53.680
Pack a broad base.

20
00:00:54.060 --> 00:00:58.115
Pack a snow mound about 15 centimetres wide on flat ground.

21
00:00:58.495 --> 00:01:01.900
Round the sides with mittened hands and flatten the top slightly.

22
00:01:02.280 --> 00:01:04.065
Keep the base broad and low.

23
00:01:04.445 --> 00:01:05.825
Grown-up help.

24
00:01:06.205 --> 00:01:08.305
Help pack the mound as needed.

25
00:01:09.833 --> 00:01:11.178
Step 3.

26
00:01:11.558 --> 00:01:13.273
Add two smaller balls.

27
00:01:13.653 --> 00:01:17.970
Make a middle ball about 10 centimetres wide and a head about 7 centimetres

28
00:01:17.970 --> 00:01:18.278
wide.

29
00:01:18.658 --> 00:01:21.088
An adult helps set them on the base.

30
00:01:21.468 --> 00:01:25.208
Press a little snow into the joins so the stack stays still.

31
00:01:25.588 --> 00:01:26.968
Grown-up help.

32
00:01:27.348 --> 00:01:29.298
Lift and steady the sections.

33
00:01:30.833 --> 00:01:31.983
Step 4.

34
00:01:32.363 --> 00:01:34.393
Press a face and add arms.

35
00:01:34.773 --> 00:01:38.183
Use the blunt twig to press shallow eyes and a smile.

36
00:01:38.563 --> 00:01:42.380
An adult may instead place a few short, blunt twigs lightly in the surface

37
00:01:42.380 --> 00:01:43.743
for a nose or mouth.

38
00:01:44.123 --> 00:01:47.488
Press two short twigs gently into the sides for arms.

39
00:01:47.868 --> 00:01:51.068
Keep the face simple and every piece removable.

40
00:01:51.448 --> 00:01:52.828
Grown-up help.

41
00:01:53.208 --> 00:01:56.333
Check twig ends and place any facial pieces.

42
00:01:57.833 --> 00:01:59.008
Step 5.

43
00:01:59.388 --> 00:02:01.038
Meet your snowy friend.

44
00:02:01.418 --> 00:02:04.803
Give the snowman a name and look at it from different sides.

45
00:02:05.183 --> 00:02:09.293
Collect the tool and remove every twig from the face and arms when finished.

46
00:02:09.673 --> 00:02:12.363
Leave only clean snow and take a warm-up break.

47
00:02:12.743 --> 00:02:14.123
Grown-up help.

48
00:02:14.503 --> 00:02:18.463
Check comfort, collect materials and return indoors when needed.

49
00:02:20.000 --> 00:02:22.915
Here are three ideas for your finished project.

50
00:02:23.295 --> 00:02:26.845
These example pictures were made with artificial intelligence.

51
00:02:27.225 --> 00:02:29.245
Your creation can look different.

52
00:02:29.625 --> 00:02:33.345
Remove all twigs, tools and other added pieces before leaving.

53
00:02:33.725 --> 00:02:37.570
Enjoy the changing snow shape where permitted; it will melt.

54
00:02:37.950 --> 00:02:38.940
Well done.

55
00:02:39.320 --> 00:02:41.750
Take a moment to enjoy what you made.

